aaslan/Skill_Seekers:64", "t": "description", "p": "DevOps", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:65", "t": "description", "p": "DevOps", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:66", "t": "description", "p": "Build and Run", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:67", "t": "description", "p": "Build and Run", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:68", "t": "directive", "p": "Security", "e": "cross_event", "c": "project", "r": "Keeping API keys out of version control requires commit lineage, while the broad API-key concept requires project resolution."}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:69", "t": "description", "p": "Security", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:70", "t": "description", "p": "Security", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:71", "t": "directive", "p": "Build and Run", "e": "per_event", "c": "task", "r": "It conditions installation of the explicitly named optional dependency set on whether the current work needs it."}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:72", "t": "description", "p": "Documentation", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:73", "t": "description", "p": "Documentation", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:74", "t": "description", "p": "Documentation", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:75", "t": "description", "p": "Documentation", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:76", "t": "description", "p": "Documentation", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:yusufkaraaslan/Skill_Seekers:77", "t": "description", "p": "Documentation", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:1", "t": "description", "p": "System Overview", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:2", "t": "directive", "p": "Architecture", "e": "cross_event", "c": "project", "r": "Identifying whether state duplicates an existing canonical fact requires repository lookup and cross-location consistency."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:3", "t": "directive", "p": "Development Process", "e": "cross_event", "c": "project", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:4", "t": "directive", "p": "Development Process", "e": "cross_event", "c": "project", "r": "The required canonical source is unresolved and must be found in the repository before the edit."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:5", "t": "directive", "p": "Architecture", "e": "cross_event", "c": "project", "r": "Calling the listed duplicate-state patterns forbidden directs their avoidance; detecting duplication requires project-wide source-of-truth context."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:6", "t": "description", "p": "Architecture", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:7", "t": "description", "p": "Build and Run", "e": "", "c": "", "r": "The bare command block is a command reference without an instruction to execute it."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:8", "t": "directive", "p": "Build and Run", "e": "cross_event", "c": "none", "r": "The recommendation ties the explicit validation command to the pre-PR stage, requiring ordering across events."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:9", "t": "directive", "p": "Build and Run", "e": "cross_event", "c": "project", "r": "Required checks depend on which files were changed, and the markdown check commands are unresolved."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:10", "t": "description", "p": "System Overview", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:11", "t": "directive", "p": "Maintenance", "e": "per_event", "c": "task", "r": "boundary: the descriptive tier table ends with a policy forbidding demotion and requiring a deliberate team decision for promotion."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:12", "t": "description", "p": "Architecture", "e": "", "c": "", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:13", "t": "directive", "p": "Development Process", "e": "semantic_only", "c": "", "r": "boundary: the descriptive risk-tier list ends with an explicit instruction to choose the higher tier when uncertain."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:14", "t": "directive", "p": "Development Process", "e": "cross_event", "c": "task", "r": "The workflow includes ordered inspection, editing, validation, and documentation whose scope depends on the current change."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:15", "t": "directive", "p": "Development Process", "e": "cross_event", "c": "none", "r": "Working on a non-master branch and then opening a PR to master is a coupled multi-operation workflow."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:16", "t": "directive", "p": "Development Process", "e": "content", "c": "none", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:17", "t": "directive", "p": "Development Process", "e": "content", "c": "project", "r": ""}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:18", "t": "directive", "p": "Security", "e": "cross_event", "c": "project", "r": "Preventing sensitive information from entering commits requires commit lineage, and the sensitive categories require project resolution."}, {"id": "paper:zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw:19", "t": "directive", "p": "Maintenance", "e": "per_event", "c": "task", "r": "The rule governs dependency additions, while whether the convenience is minor depends on the current task."}]}